<title>UK: Zeneca surges to record high on bid talk.</title>
<headline>Zeneca surges to record high on bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continued rumours of a bid for UK pharmaceutical firm Zeneca Group Plc, this time from Germany's Bayer AG sent shares soaring to record highs on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>A 71-1/2p rise took shares through the 16.00 stg barrier to a new peak of 16.15 stg.</p>
<p>Rumours of a bid for Zeneca have abounded since its split from ICI three years ago though none has yet be shown to have any substance.</p>
<p>&quot;Fund managers feel they can't not own Zeneca. They either buy more or hold what they've got,&quot; said an analyst.  </p>
<p>&quot;They don't feel selling is an option,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
